PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
Deliberation has coalesced around three main pathways: federal statutory admission (25 or 26 states), direct Article V thresholds (38 or 39 states), and adversarial voter migration to state legislatures (4, 15, or 26 states). The federal statutory route faces a fatal flaw because staggered six-year Senate terms prevent guaranteed legislative turnover within 51 months, whereas the 51-month timeframe precisely matches the four-year cycle of all state legislative chambers plus convening time. Furthermore, the explicit inclusion of the Federal District and Puerto Rico defines the adversarial population pool in a relocation game, making the Colonel Blotto formulation of 15 states the most mathematically consistent adversarial equilibrium.
}

